# Drafted by Gemini (R20), edited. R20 side quest: A Jury of Pigeons. Tamsin Ledger will not let a mob try anyone without a docket, a quorum and sworn witnesses.

~ start
Narrator: Tamsin Ledger perches on an overturned crate at the edge of the Round, clipboard balanced on her knee. Her pen scratches steadily through the torchsmoke, auditing the howling mob as if it were a column of bad sums.
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: This riot is entirely out of order: no docket, no quorum, and not a single sworn witness. I am taking the minutes regardless, and since I require an impartial jury, you four are hereby drafted.
* We'll sit on your jury. -> accept
* What is the charge? -> charge
* We have no time for a mock trial. -> END

~ charge
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: As near as I can tell from the shouting, the charge is being a pigeon. I have yet to establish whether that is a statutory offence in Wickermoor.
-> start

~ accept
set rk_jury_asked
quest jury_of_pigeons asked
tamsin_ledger [smile]: Very good, I have ticked the box. I require a ruled docket, a seated quorum, and an oath from the witnesses, preferably before the Witching Hour.
-> END

~ progress
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Let us consult the checklist: a docket, a quorum, and a binding oath. Tell me which irregularity we are correcting next.
-> menu

~ menu
* [if not flag.rk_jury_docket] Let's get a docket from Mayor Somerton. -> docket
* [if not flag.rk_jury_quorum] Let's seat a quorum from the crowd. -> quorum
* [if not flag.rk_jury_oath] Let's swear in the pigeons as witnesses. -> oath
* [if flag.rk_jury_docket and flag.rk_jury_quorum and flag.rk_jury_oath] Call the hearing to order. -> hearing
* [ends:jury_of_pigeons] Give it up. This hearing is hopeless. -> quit
* We'll come back to the audit later. -> END

~ docket
* [Persuasion DC 13] Ask Mayor Somerton politely for an official docket form. -> docket_ok | docket_poor
* Copy a blank docket by hand from his desk. -> docket_copy
~ docket_poor
Narrator: Mayor Somerton waxes his moustache and informs you through the barred casement that blank forms are issued on Thursdays only.
-> menu
~ docket_copy
time +60
-> docket_ok
~ docket_ok
set rk_jury_docket
give rk_docket
Narrator: The crisp, ruled paper smells faintly of iron gall and municipal dust. Tamsin's eyes follow the blank docket in your hand like a hawk watching a fieldmouse.
-> menu

~ quorum
* [Intimidation DC 12] Order the mob to sit down in proper rows. -> quorum_ok | quorum_poor
* Point out that the village goat counts toward a quorum. -> quorum_goat
~ quorum_poor
Narrator: Pitchforks shift and lilac eyes stare straight through you. Clearly, nobody has told them they are dismissed.
-> menu
~ quorum_goat
Narrator: Tamsin peers at the chewing goat, consults a footnote on her clipboard, and marks the beast down as a ratepayer in good standing.
-> quorum_ok
~ quorum_ok
set rk_jury_quorum
Narrator: By some miracle of stubborn habit, twelve villagers fold their knees and sit in crooked rows upon the cold cobbles, torches held upright like bailiffs' staves.
-> menu

~ oath
* [Animal Handling DC 12] Coax a pigeon onto your arm to take the oath. -> oath_ok | oath_poor
* [Performance DC 12] Swear the roof-pigeons in with a grand, solemn flourish. -> oath_ok | oath_poor
* Request a solemn affirmation from the birds instead. -> oath_affirm
~ oath_poor
Narrator: The fat grey bird fixes you with one bright orange eye, ruffles its neck, and leaves a warm white deposit squarely in the margin of the docket.
-> menu
~ oath_affirm
Narrator: Tamsin lowers her pen, consults the parish bylaws, and notes that under section nine a solemn affirmation is equally binding upon poultry and waterfowl.
-> oath_ok
~ oath_ok
set rk_jury_oath
Narrator: A low, bubbling coo ripples along the slate eaves, and Tamsin's pen scratches it into the record as a unanimous assent.
-> menu

~ hearing
quest jury_of_pigeons sitting
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: This sitting of the Wickermoor Assizes is now in session. The accused stands charged with willful and habitual pigeonry: has the bird anything to say before we proceed?
Narrator: The grey cock on the roof-beam puffs his crop and warbles a long, liquid cadence. Torchlight wavers over silent faces as the villagers listen, rapt, as though the bird were reciting scripture.
tamsin_ledger [smile]: A weighty deposition, I am sure, yet the bylaw is quite clear. No verdict may be entered until the prior minutes are read aloud in full, beginning with page one.
set rk_mob_calm = now
set rk_jury_done
quest jury_of_pigeons done
Narrator: By the third page the pitch-torches are guttering in their sockets, and by the tenth the charmed villagers lie snoring in neat rows upon the stones. For the first hour in days, the Round is entirely quiet.
-> END

~ quit
set rk_jury_abandoned
quest jury_of_pigeons abandoned
tamsin_ledger [sad]: Oh. Yes, I suppose the paperwork was rather ambitious under the circumstances; I shall pack the docket away.
-> END

~ after
if flag.rk_jury_done
tamsin_ledger [smile]: You will be pleased to hear the minutes were adopted without objection. Mind you, no one was awake to second the motion.
-> END
endif
tamsin_ledger [weary]: I am still recording the irregularities, for all the good it does. Nobody in this parish ever reads the audit.
-> END
